From 45dd436e5277c7d0a211a6a0e0b14ae5657325c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MyNaai <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:50:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shop: repair the two-buyer schema at boot, and replay a
 blocked write once
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A customer checkout still died on production with

  null value in column "salon_id" of relation "shop_orders"
  violates not-null constraint

because the code shipped without migrations/2026-10-22-shop-customers.sql
being run (and `allowNull: true` in a model never alters an existing column).

- src/database/config/ensureShopBuyerSchema.js: idempotent DDL that adds
  buyer_type / customer_id to shop_orders + shop_carts and drops NOT NULL from
  salon_id on both. `IF NOT EXISTS` / `IF EXISTS` all the way, so it is a no-op
  on a migrated database and cannot affect a salon order.
- index.js: runs once after the DB connects (best-effort; a missing ALTER
  privilege logs and moves on).
- shopOrder.service.createOrder + shopCart.service.addLine: `withBuyerSchema`
  replays the write after a repair when — and only when — the failure is the
  salon_id not-null violation (23502 on that column). Other errors are
  untouched, so nothing is masked.
- Foreign keys and the cart unique index stay in the migration: they can fail
  on orphan rows and boot should not be noisy.

Proven with PGlite (two scenarios: production's half-migrated tables and a
table that never got the columns): the customer insert is rejected before,
both inserts succeed after, a second run is a no-op, salon orders work in
both states, and existing rows stay buyer_type = 'SALON'.
---
 index.js                                     |  10 +-
 src/database/config/ensureShopBuyerSchema.js | 126 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/services/shopCart.service.js             |   3 +-
 src/services/shopOrder.service.js            |   8 +-
 4 files changed, 143 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/database/config/ensureShopBuyerSchema.js

